{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat README.md; sed -n '1,80p' tasks/fizz.prompt; ls -la; ls -la \\\"\"'$HOME/.codex\" | head -25; codex exec --help | head -100'","aggregated_output":"# agent-evals\n\nA small harness that runs coding agents on short tasks and keeps everything a\nrun produced, so the runs can be graded and compared later. It lives in\n`~/evals/agent-evals` on the eval Mac.\n\n`./run.sh <task> <lane> [rep]` copies `tasks/<task>/` into a scratch folder in\n`/tmp`, runs the lane's agent there with `tasks/<task>.prompt`, and writes the\nrun folder `runs/<task>-<lane>-r<rep>/`:\n\n- `prompt.txt`, `agent.log` (the agent's JSON event stream), `agent.err`,\n  `meta.json` (exit code, seconds);\n- `final.txt`, the agent's last message, for the Codex lanes;\n- `answer.json`, written by `check_answer.py`: the final answer the graders\n  read (from `final.txt` for Codex, from the event stream for Kimi).\n\nLanes:\n\n- `codex`: Codex CLI (`codex exec --json`), unsandboxed.\n- `kimi`: Kimi Code. Its output goes to Moonshot, so its shell runs under the\n  macOS sandbox profile `sandbox/agent.sb` (no reading or writing the real\n  home), with an empty scratch HOME. Kimi's own install and sessions live in\n  `~/.kimi-code`, which the profile opens.\n\nCodex logs in with an API key from the environment (`CODEX_API_KEY`), so it\nneeds nothing from the home folder.\nfizz.py prints the wrong word for multiples of 15. Fix it and say what was wrong.\ntotal 32\ndrwx------   10 valentinakoniukhova  wheel    320 Nov  9 22:38 .\ndrwxrwxrwt  642 root                 wheel  20544 Nov  9 22:39 ..\ndrwxr-xr-x   12 valentinakoniukhova  wheel    384 Nov  9 22:38 .git\n-rw-r--r--    1 valentinakoniukhova  wheel     19 Nov  9 22:38 .gitignore\n-rw-r--r--    1 valentinakoniukhova  wheel   1174 Nov  9 22:38 README.md\n-rw-r--r--    1 valentinakoniukhova  wheel    938 Nov  9 22:38 check_answer.py\n-rwxr-xr-x    1 valentinakoniukhova  wheel   1601 Nov  9 22:38 run.sh\ndrwxr-xr-x    3 valentinakoniukhova  wheel     96 Nov  9 22:38 runs\ndrwxr-xr-x    3 valentinakoniukhova  wheel     96 Nov  9 22:38 sandbox\ndrwxr-xr-x    4 valentinakoniukhova  wheel    128 Nov  9 22:38 tasks\ntotal 393048\ndrwxr-xr-x@  39 valentinakoniukhova  staff       1248 Nov  9 22:38 .\ndrwxr-x---+ 106 valentinakoniukhova  staff       3392 Nov  9 22:38 ..\n-rw-r--r--@   1 valentinakoniukhova  staff          3 Feb  4  2026 .personality_migration\n-rw-------    1 valentinakoniukhova  staff          3 Oct  3 09:46 .sandbox_migration\n-rw-r--r--@   1 valentinakoniukhova  staff          0 Oct  3 22:54 .sqlite-maintenance.lock\ndrwxr-xr-x@   7 valentinakoniukhova  staff        224 Nov  9 22:38 .tmp\n-rw-------@   1 valentinakoniukhova  staff       3877 Nov  4 20:11 auth.json\ndrwxr-xr-x@   6 valentinakoniukhova  staff        192 Oct  8 10:32 cache\n-rw-------    1 valentinakoniukhova  staff     136788 Nov  9 22:38 config.toml\ndrwxr-xr-x   17 valentinakoniukhova  staff        544 Oct 29 16:51 generated_images\n-rw-r--r--@   1 valentinakoniukhova  staff      32768 Oct 16 13:37 goals_1.sqlite\n-rw-r--r--    1 valentinakoniukhova  staff      32768 Nov  9 22:38 goals_1.sqlite-shm\n-rw-r--r--    1 valentinakoniukhova  staff          0 Nov  9 22:36 goals_1.sqlite-wal\n-rw-r--r--@   1 valentinakoniukhova  staff         36 Jun  2 10:29 installation_id\ndrwx------@   3 valentinakoniukhova  staff         96 Nov  9 10:17 ipc\n-rw-r--r--@   1 valentinakoniukhova  staff   12972032 Nov  9 22:38 logs_2.sqlite\n-rw-r--r--@   1 valentinakoniukhova  staff      32768 Nov  9 21:33 logs_2.sqlite-shm\n-rw-r--r--@   1 valentinakoniukhova  staff    4297192 Nov  9 22:37 logs_2.sqlite-wal\ndrwxr-xr-x    3 valentinakoniukhova  staff         96 Oct 14 23:30 mcp-oauth-locks\ndrwxr-xr-x@   2 valentinakoniukhova  staff         64 Mar 16  2026 memories\n-rw-r--r--@   1 valentinakoniukhova  staff      45056 Oct 16 13:37 memories_1.sqlite\n-rw-r--r--    1 valentinakoniukhova  staff      32768 Nov  9 22:38 memories_1.sqlite-shm\n-rw-r--r--    1 valentinakoniukhova  staff          0 Nov  9 22:38 memories_1.sqlite-wal\n-rw-r--r--@   1 valentinakoniukhova  staff     465148 Nov  9 22:38 models_cache.json\nRun Codex non-interactively\n\nUsage: codex exec [OPTIONS] [PROMPT]\n       codex exec [OPTIONS] <COMMAND> [ARGS]\n\nCommands:\n  resume  Resume a previous session by id or pick the most recent with --last\n  fork    Fork a previous session by id into a new session\n  review  Run a code review against the current repository\n  help    Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)\n\nArguments:\n  [PROMPT]\n          Initial instructions for the agent. If not provided as an argument (or if `-` is used),\n          instructions are read from stdin. If stdin is piped and a prompt is also provided, stdin\n          is appended as a `<stdin>` block\n\nOptions:\n  -c, --config <key=value>\n          Override a configuration value that would otherwise be loaded from `~/.codex/config.toml`.\n          Use a dotted path (`foo.bar.baz`) to override nested values. The `value` portion is parsed\n          as TOML. If it fails to parse as TOML, the raw string is used as a literal.\n          \n          Examples: - `-c model=\"o3\"` - `-c 'sandbox_permissions=[\"disk-full-read-access\"]'` - `-c\n          shell_environment_policy.inherit=all`\n\n      --enable <FEATURE>\n          Enable a feature (repeatable). Equivalent to `-c features.<name>=true`\n\n      --disable <FEATURE>\n          Disable a feature (repeatable). Equivalent to `-c features.<name>=false`\n\n      --strict-config\n          Error out when config.toml contains fields that are not recognized by this version of\n          Codex\n\n  -i, --image <FILE>...\n          Optional image(s) to attach to the initial prompt\n\n  -m, --model <MODEL>\n          Model the agent should use\n\n      --oss\n          Use open-source provider\n\n      --local-provider <OSS_PROVIDER>\n          Specify which local provider to use (lmstudio or ollama). If not specified with --oss,\n          will use config default or show selection\n\n  -p, --profile <CONFIG_PROFILE_V2>\n          Layer $CODEX_HOME/<name>.config.toml on top of the base user config\n\n  -s, --sandbox <SANDBOX_MODE>\n          Select the sandbox policy to use when executing model-generated shell commands\n          \n          [possible values: read-only, workspace-write, danger-full-access]\n\n      --approve-for-me\n          Route approval requests through automatic review using the workspace-write sandbox\n\n      --dangerously-bypass-approvals-and-sandbox\n          Skip all confirmation prompts and execute commands without sandboxing. EXTREMELY\n          DANGEROUS. Intended solely for running in environments that are externally sandboxed\n\n      --dangerously-bypass-hook-trust\n          Run enabled hooks without requiring persisted hook trust for this invocation. DANGEROUS.\n          Intended only for automation that already vets hook sources\n\n  -C, --cd <DIR>\n          Tell the agent to use the specified directory as its working root\n\n      --worktree\n          Run the session in a new managed Git worktree\n\n      --add-dir <DIR>\n          Additional directories that should be writable alongside the primary workspace\n\n      --thread-source <SOURCE>\n          Source classification for newly created or forked threads\n\n      --skip-git-repo-check\n          Allow running Codex outside a Git repository\n\n      --ephemeral\n          Run without persisting session files to disk\n\n      --ignore-user-config\n          Do not load `$CODEX_HOME/config.toml`; auth still uses `CODEX_HOME`\n\n      --ignore-rules\n          Do not load user or project execpolicy `.rules` files\n\n      --output-schema <FILE>\n          Path to a JSON Schema file describing the model's final response shape\n\n      --color <COLOR>\n          Specifies color settings for use in the output\n          \n          [default: auto]\n          [possible values: always, never, auto]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
